Notes:
This challenge contained multiple red herrings, including an encrypted flag file that was not immediately useful. I inspected the Python source code using nano and found that the password was stored in hexadecimal format. After converting the hex value to ASCII, I obtained the correct password, entered it into the program, and successfully revealed the flag. This challenge reinforced the importance of carefully analysing source code and recognising different data encodings.

